[8] In summarizing its findings, the RPD concluded that the Applicant had not provided, on a balance of probabilities, sufficient credible evidence to support her allegations:
No summons had been issued;
The Applicant had not established her allegation that fellow villagers were detained, even if arrested;
There was insufficient credible evidence upon which to make a finding that the PSB were pursing the Applicant;
There was insufficient credible evidence upon which to make a finding that the Minor Applicant was, in fact, dismissed from his school; and
There was insufficient credible evidence with respect to the property concerned.

